 35S     34S(N,N),(N,G):RESONANCES     1984CA14,2018MUZY         ENSDF    202509
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35S 2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35S 2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35S  c  2018MuZY: evaluation of neutron resonance energies, J|p values, width  
 35S 2c  parameters, and resonance strengths for nuclei of Z=1-60.              
 35S  c  1984Ca14: 30-1500-keV neutrons were produced from the Oak Ridge        
 35S 2c  Electron Linear Accelerator (ORELA). The target was 94.33%-enriched    
 35S 3c  {+34}S with a 5.54% impurity of {+32}S. Neutrons were detected using a 
 35S 4c  2-cm-thick and 7.5-cm in diameter NE110 proton-recoil detector. Prompt 
 35S 5c  |g rays from neutron capture are detected using two nonhydrogenous     
 35S 6c  fluorocarbon scintillators (NE-226). Measured |s(E{-n}). Deduced 81    
 35S 7c  resonances, J, |p, L, widths and spectroscopic factors by comparing the
 35S 8c  R-matrix predictions of the cross section with the data.               
 35S  cL $All resonance parameters including resonance neutron energies, J, L,  
 35S 2cL g|G{-n}, |G{-|g}, and resonance strengths are from the compilation and 
 35S 3cL evaluation in 2018MuZY, unless otherwise noted.                        
 35S  cL $g|G{-n}=(2J+1)|G{-n}/2.                                               
